# L5R 5E — ERRATA & FAQ (LORE): KISSHŌTEN, FORTUNE OF HAPPINESS, FERTILITY, AND BEAUTY

**Version:** 0.4.1
**Source:** Legend of the Five Rings Roleplaying Game, 5th Edition — Errata & FAQ (v20, 2019-09-25 and 2020-08-12)
**Publisher:** Fantasy Flight Games

> Errata-restored setting entry. Kisshōten is listed among the Eight Great Fortunes in the
> core rulebook but was omitted from *Emerald Empire*. Per the official FAQ, that omission is an
> in-world act rather than an editorial one — this file restores Kisshōten's entry to the canonical
> roster of Great Fortunes. Verbatim from the core rulebook's "Eight Great Fortunes" sidebar and the
> Errata & FAQ.

---

## The Eight Great Fortunes

**EIGHT GREAT FORTUNES** (from left to right)

- Bishamon: Fortune of Strength
- Fukurokujin: Fortune of Wisdom and Mercy
- Kisshōten: Fortune of Happiness, Fertility, and Beauty
- Ebisu: Fortune of Honest Work
- Daikoku: Fortune of Wealth
- Benten: Fortune of Arts and Romantic Love
- Hotei: Fortune of Contentment
- Jurōjin: Fortune of Longevity

## FAQ

**Q: Why is Kisshōten noted as one of the Eight Great Fortunes in the core rulebook, but isn't in Emerald Empire?**

A: Kisshōten is widely considered one of the Eight Great Fortunes, though some in Rokugan disagree. Those dissenters managed to remove Kisshōten's entry from Emerald Empire.
